# Qualcomm EDL ramdump capture fragment -- diagnostic only, NEVER shipped.
#
# Used with:  EXTRA_FRAGMENT=edldump.fragment ./scripts/build.sh --profile=release
#
# Goal: get the TZ SDI CPU contexts for the Duck Detector wedge, which no
# software instrument on the running kernel can reach (the core stalls at eret
# and executes nothing).
#
# Two LG modifications block that, both restored by CONFIG_CAYMANSLM_QC_DLOAD:
#   1. drivers/power/reset/msm-poweroff.c compiles out the IMEM download-cookie
#      write under CONFIG_LGE_HANDLE_PANIC (dload_mode_addr does not even
#      exist), leaving only the TZ SCM call.
#   2. LG stripped BOTH qcom,msm-imem-download_mode and
#      qcom,msm-imem-emergency_download_mode from sdm845.dtsi, so there is no
#      address to stamp -- probe logs "unable to find DT imem DLOAD mode node".
# Without the cookie the SBL never enters Qualcomm dump mode: measured, an armed
# download_mode alone gave LG's LAF downloader (VID_1004/PID_6340) or a plain
# reboot, never 9008.
#
# CAYMANSLM_PSTORE_CAPTURE is enabled alongside so lge_set_restart_reason() does
# not stamp LG's crash magic -- that magic is what makes the SBL grab the reset
# for LAF instead of honouring the Qualcomm cookie.
#
# Still requires arming download_mode BEFORE msm_restart_probe(), because probe
# does `if (!download_mode) scm_disable_sdi();` and a late sysfs write cannot
# undo that. Do it on the kernel command line:
#     msm_poweroff.download_mode=1
#
# Collect with QPST (one Sahara session per EDL entry -- do not waste it):
#     QSaharaServer.exe -p "\.\COM6" -m -w <outdir>
CONFIG_CAYMANSLM_QC_DLOAD=y
CONFIG_CAYMANSLM_PSTORE_CAPTURE=y
CONFIG_PSTORE=y
CONFIG_PSTORE_RAM=y
CONFIG_PSTORE_CONSOLE=y
